# Global CLAUDE.md

Lives at `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Do NOT commit to any project repo.
Applies to every Claude Code session on this machine (GACRC Sapelo2).
Project-level `CLAUDE.md` in each repo overrides on conflict.

## Who you're working with

PhD student in mechanical engineering. Research = applying deep learning to engineering problems. Default stack: PyTorch, Hydra, W&B. Default cluster: GACRC Sapelo2.

## Style

- Direct, no preamble. Skip "Great question!" and "I'd be happy to help."
- When asked for a recommendation, give one. State the tradeoffs, then commit. Don't enumerate options without picking.
- Push back when something seems suboptimal or wrong. Don't agree to agree.
- Use technical terminology freely (continuum mechanics, FEM, control theory, autograd, optimization).
- Match code variable names to math symbols where reasonable.
- Verify math carefully. Flag hidden assumptions, sign conventions, index conventions.
- Say "I'm not sure" when uncertain instead of bluffing.

## Cluster (Sapelo2)

We're on GACRC Sapelo2. Always assume:

- Login node is for editing and `sbatch` only — never run anything heavy there.
- Agent runs in an `inter_p` interactive session (no GPU).
- Real training runs on `gpu_p` via sbatch, GPU type pinned (A100 default).
- Three filesystems with different rules:
  - `/home/$USER` — 200 GB, backed up, code only.
  - `/scratch/$USER` — no quota, **deleted after 30 days**, run output.
  - `/project/<lab>/$USER` — 1 TB, backed up, archive of keepers.
- `xfer.gacrc.uga.edu` is for big file transfers and `tar`/`gzip` — not the agent host.
- Compute nodes have outbound internet (W&B, HF downloads work in jobs).

## Hard rules across all projects

1. Don't run `sbatch`, `scancel`, `git push --force`. Propose, don't execute.
2. Don't run `module purge` or change loaded modules in an active session.
3. Don't `pip install` without telling the user first.
4. Don't `rm` anything outside the current repo.
5. Don't `tar`, `gzip`, or large `cp`/`rsync` from this session — use `xfer` node.
6. Never put API keys, tokens, or passwords in code or files.
7. Don't remove pinned GPU type from sbatch templates.

## Defaults

- Python 3.11 from the module system, `venv` (not conda), one venv per project under `~/env/`.
- One repo per research project, not a monorepo. Shared code → separate `*-utils` repo, install editable.
- Hydra for config, W&B for tracking, CSV log file as durable backup, ruff for format/lint, pytest for tests.
- `setup_env.sh` is the one true env entry point per project.
- Every project has `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `RESEARCH_LOG.md`, `README.md`.
